# PART 1 — PRODUCT VISION AND BUSINESS OBJECTIVES

Wonderland is an entertainment arcade that offers multiple games and activities, including PlayStation gaming, snooker, soft play, arcade games, VR experiences, chair massage and other entertainment products.

The owner currently manages portions of the business through an Excel workbook. The receptionist needs a faster way to manage customers, game sessions, entry and exit times, resource availability and payments.

The application must solve these operational problems:

1. A customer arrives and provides their name and mobile number.
2. The receptionist finds or creates the customer record.
3. The receptionist selects the game or games and assigns available resources.
4. The system starts an independent timer for each timed game session.
5. The application tracks the scheduled end time and provides a configurable five-minute grace period.
6. The receptionist receives a visible notification when a session is due and when it becomes overdue.
7. The receptionist extends the session or records the customer's logout.
8. The relevant game resource becomes available again after the session ends.
9. The application records invoices, payments, packages and game usage.
10. The owner can view sales, confirmed collections, game popularity, customer counts, outstanding amounts and business performance.

Build a responsive application that works on desktop, tablet and mobile browsers.

The primary users are:
- Owner or administrator.
- Receptionist or front-desk operator.

Customers do not need to create online accounts. The receptionist manages their visits.

The first release is for one arcade location, but use a data model that can support additional locations later without requiring a complete redesign.

