## UPI automation

Investigate an official merchant payment-provider API, payment webhook or authorized bank reconciliation method before proposing direct SMS ingestion.

Do not assume that a browser can read incoming SMS messages.

Do not bypass device permissions or collect the entire SMS history.

If direct SMS ingestion is required, treat it as a separately designed native Android integration subject to platform permissions, compliance requirements and distribution feasibility. It must not be a dependency for the web application.

Do not confirm a payment merely because an SMS contains a similar amount.

Prefer a verified provider event or authorized reconciliation source.

When a reliable transaction match is unavailable, place the transaction in a Pending Reconciliation queue.

Prevent duplicate messages or repeated webhooks from creating duplicate payment records.

Store a unique source transaction identifier or reference where available.

Validate payment source, amount, status, timestamp and transaction identity.

Do not match transactions solely by amount and approximate time when multiple payments could be candidates.

Keep unconfirmed and unmatched transactions out of confirmed-receipt totals.

For a zero-cost initial release, implement reliable manual payment recording and an optional controlled transaction-import workflow. Keep the architecture ready for a future official payment integration.

Do not store UPI PINs, banking passwords, card security codes or unnecessary sensitive banking data.

