# PART 17 — FINAL COMPLETION REQUIREMENTS

The finished application must provide the following complete workflows:

### Workflow A: Walk-in customer

Register or find a customer, select a game, assign a resource, select duration, start the timer, display the countdown, receive expiry alerts, extend the session or log out the customer, and preserve history.

### Workflow B: Multiple games

Allow one customer visit to contain separate PS5, snooker or other game sessions, each with independent timing and resource assignment.

### Workflow C: Packages

Sell a package, record the invoice and payment, create a customer entitlement, track validity and minutes, deduct usage and show the remaining balance.

### Workflow D: Checkout

Create an invoice from eligible products or sessions, record payments, calculate outstanding balances and preserve a financial audit trail.

### Workflow E: Owner dashboard

Show accurate sales, confirmed receipts, payment methods, sessions, unique customers, game-wise usage and outstanding amounts for the selected period.

### Workflow F: Reconciliation

Import or receive supported payment transaction data, prevent duplication, match transactions when supported, and route uncertain cases to manual review.

### Workflow G: Notifications

Display due and overdue alerts, preserve pending notifications, and use optional external notification integrations without making them essential to core session operations.

### Workflow H: Administration

Manage users, games, products, rates, physical resources, packages, settings, imports and reports according to permissions.

### Workflow I: Deployment and recovery

Deploy the frontend, connect the backend, configure authentication, validate security, back up business data and document restoration.

